new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..49b731a6abbcdbd611b6e78dab82160b06a39bc5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOSH_COMPLETION_PATCH.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# nosh completion delta
+
+Based on official `reubeno/brush` commit
+`96a26d0c66cbc018a1517e9562944418fef5b272`
+(`brush-core-v0.5.0`). The parser remains at its matching official 0.4.0 source.
+The original MIT license is retained.
+
+The delta exposes specification selection and existing completion tokenization,
+allows specification generation without silently appending fallback candidates,
+and returns effective `compopt` settings. nosh decides candidate sources before
+matching; native enumeration and fuzzy ranking are not injected into scripts.
+
+Completion function errors and exhausted restart limits propagate instead of
+becoming empty successful results. Temporary `COMP_*`, `COMPREPLY`, trap delivery
+and in-flight option state are restored. Dynamic `nosort` is honored; directory
+fallback is conditional rather than always mixed into a nonempty specification.
+
+`-C` output is bounded while reading. Failed completion commands and output
+overflow are real errors. The normal command-substitution output API remains
+unchanged.
+
+The serde completion execution snapshot borrows environment/functions rather
+than cloning them in the live shell. Restore occurs only in a separate completion
+host, with its own builtin implementations, null I/O, no history/job control and
+no inherited custom descriptors. Actual state includes arrays, attributes,
+function source information, aliases, options, traps, completion configuration,
+hashes, positional arguments and cwd. nosh owns snapshot size limits, workers,
+process ownership, cancellation, health and cache policy.
+
+These APIs do not sandbox arbitrary programmable completion. No changes are
+made to ordinary user command execution or the maintained parser's grammar.
